DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk()  function  locks  the spin lock referred to by
       _l_o_c_k.  If the spin lock is currently unlocked, the calling  thread  ac‐
       quires  the  lock immediately.  If the spin lock is currently locked by
       another thread, the calling thread spins, testing the lock until it be‐
       comes available, at which point the calling thread acquires the lock.

       Calling pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk() on a lock  that  is  already  held  by  the
       caller    or    a   lock   that   has   not   been   initialized   with
       pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt(3) results in undefined behavior.

       The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() function is like pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk(), except
       that if the spin lock referred to by _l_o_c_k is  currently  locked,  then,
       instead of spinning, the call returns immediately with the error EEBBUUSSYY.

       The  pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk()  function  unlocks the spin lock referred to
       _l_o_c_k.  If any threads are spinning on the lock, one  of  those  threads
       will then acquire the lock.

       Calling  pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk() on a lock that is not held by the caller
       results in undefined behavior.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return zero.  On failure,  they  return  an
       error number.

EERRRROORRSS
       pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk() may fail with the following errors:

       EEDDEEAADDLLOOCCKK
              The system detected a deadlock condition.

       pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ttrryylloocckk() fails with the following errors:

       EEBBUUSSYY  The spin lock is currently locked by another thread.

